    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always felt like a distant language to me. While I appreciate its logic and structure, my primary connection comes through computer science, where numbers and algorithms feel more practical than abstract theory. I see it as a tool rather than a passion, often relying on others for deeper understanding.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, absolutely. The pressure to understand complex formulas or solve problems quickly can trigger real anxiety. My low extraversion and high agreeableness make me worry about disappointing others if I struggle. It's not fear of failure, but fear of being perceived as incapable.",
